_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 8
---
order: 8
---
short_label: VII.8
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If a number is the same parts of a number that a subtracted number is of a subtracted number, then the remainder is also the same parts of the remainder that the whole is of the whole.
----
proof:

Let the number {AB} be the same parts of the number {CD} that {AE} subtracted is of {CF} subtracted.

I say that the remainder {EB} is also the same parts of the remainder {FD} that the whole {AB} is of the whole {CD}.

<figure class="diagram rdiagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="280" height="150" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VII.8 diagram" src="propVII8.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // AB is parts of CD, AE the same parts of CF (E and F cut AB and CD in
    // the ratio 2:3 through the P0…P3 helper). GH is made equal to AB, K
    // halves it, L halves AE, and M, N are laid off for the two VII.7
    // steps. Line segments only, so the walk is highlight beats, with G and
    // GH, then K, L, M, N appearing with the sentences that make them.
    //
    // Added to Joyce's figure, all transparent (;0;0;0): the segments AE,
    // EB, CF, FD, GK, KH, AL, LE, GM, MK, KN and NH the proof names, so
    // they can light.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): the lineSliders A, B, C, D,
    // G and the colourless off-canvas helpers C0…A3, P0, P1. G is the end
    // of GH, which the proof makes mid-walk, so it is deferred. E, F, H,
    // K, L, M, N are derived and follow the visible sets.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","E","AB","AE","EB","C","D","F","CD","CF","FD"];
    var MADE  = GIVEN.concat(["G","H","GH"]);
    var DIVK  = MADE.concat(["K","GK","KH"]);
    var DIVL  = DIVK.concat(["L","AL","LE"]);
    var CUTM  = DIVL.concat(["M","GM"]);
    var REMM  = CUTM.concat(["MK"]);
    var CUTN  = REMM.concat(["N","KN"]);
    var REMN  = CUTN.concat(["NH"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "VII.8",
        elements: [
            "C0;point;free;-1000,40;0;0",
            "C3;point;free;1000,40;0;0",
            "G0;point;free;-1000,75;0;0",
            "G3;point;free;1000,75;0;0",
            "A0;point;free;-1000,110;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,110;0;0",
            "A;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,40,110",
            "B;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,200,110",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "C;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,40,40",
            "D;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,240,110",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D",
            "P0;point;free;1000,1000;0;0",
            "P1;point;free;1000,1100;0;0",
            "P2;point;extend;P0,P1,P0,P1;0;0",
            "P3;point;extend;P1,P2,P0,P1;0;0",
            "E;point;proportion;P0,P3,P0,P2,A,B,A,B",
            "F;point;proportion;P0,P3,P0,P2,C,D,C,D",
            "G;point;lineSlider;G0,G3,40,75",
            "H;point;cutoff;G,G3,A,B",
            "GH;line;connect;G,H",
            "K;point;midpoint;G,H",
            "L;point;midpoint;A,E",
            "M;point;cutoff;G,H,A,L",
            "N;point;cutoff;K,H,E,B",
            // Invisible highlight targets. Zero-colour: nothing changes at rest.
            "AE;line;connect;A,E;0;0;0",
            "EB;line;connect;E,B;0;0;0",
            "CF;line;connect;C,F;0;0;0",
            "FD;line;connect;F,D;0;0;0",
            "GK;line;connect;G,K;0;0;0",
            "KH;line;connect;K,H;0;0;0",
            "AL;line;connect;A,L;0;0;0",
            "LE;line;connect;L,E;0;0;0",
            "GM;line;connect;G,M;0;0;0",
            "MK;line;connect;M,K;0;0;0",
            "KN;line;connect;K,N;0;0;0",
            "NH;line;connect;N,H;0;0;0"
        ],
        deferDraggables: ["G"],
        aliases: { "BA": "AB", "DC": "CD", "BE": "EB", "DF": "FD", "HG": "GH",
                   "HK": "KH", "EL": "LE", "KM": "MK", "HN": "NH" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“If a number is the same parts of a number that a subtracted number is of a subtracted number,”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","AE","CF"] },
            { text: "“then the remainder is also the same parts of the remainder that the whole is of the whole.”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["EB","FD","AB","CD"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VII.8" }] },
            { text: "Let the number {AB} be the same parts of the number {CD}",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD"] },
            { text: "that {AE} subtracted is of {CF} subtracted.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AE","CF"] },
            { text: "I say that the remainder {EB} is also the same parts of the remainder {FD}",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["EB","FD"] },
            { text: "that the whole {AB} is of the whole {CD}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD"] },
            { text: "Make {GH} equal to {AB}.",
              visible: MADE,
              highlighted: ["GH","AB"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "G", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "GH", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Therefore {AE} is the same parts of {CF} that {GH} is of {CD}.",
              visible: MADE,
              highlighted: ["AE","CF","GH","CD"] },
            { text: "Divide {GH} into the parts of {CD}, namely {GK} and {KH},",
              visible: DIVK,
              highlighted: ["GK","KH","K"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "K", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "and divide {AE} into the parts of {CF}, namely {AL} and {LE}.",
              visible: DIVL,
              highlighted: ["AL","LE","L"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "L", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "Then the multitude of {GK} and {KH} equals the multitude of {AL} and {LE}.",
              visible: DIVL,
              highlighted: ["GK","KH","AL","LE"] },
            { text: "Now since {AL} is the same part of {CF} that {GK} is of {CD},",
              visible: DIVL,
              highlighted: ["AL","CF","GK","CD"] },
            { text: "and {CD} is greater than {CF}, therefore {GK} is also greater than {AL}.",
              visible: DIVL,
              highlighted: ["CD","CF","GK","AL"] },
            { text: "Make {GM} equal to {AL}.",
              visible: CUTM,
              highlighted: ["GM","AL","M"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "M", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "Then {GK} is the same part of {CD} that {GM} is of {CF}.",
              visible: CUTM,
              highlighted: ["GK","CD","GM","CF"] },
            { text: "Therefore the remainder {MK} is the same part of the remainder {FD}",
              visible: REMM,
              highlighted: ["MK","FD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "MK is the same part of FD", ref: "VII.7" }] },
            { text: "that the whole {GK} is of the whole {CD}.",
              visible: REMM,
              highlighted: ["GK","CD"] },
            { text: "Again, since {EL} is the same part of {CF} that {KH} is of {CD},",
              visible: REMM,
              highlighted: ["LE","CF","KH","CD"] },
            { text: "and {CD} is greater than {CF}, therefore {HK} is also greater than {EL}.",
              visible: REMM,
              highlighted: ["CD","CF","KH","LE"] },
            { text: "Make {KN} equal to {EL}.",
              visible: CUTN,
              highlighted: ["KN","LE","N"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "N", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "Therefore {KN} is the same part of {CF} that {KH} is of {CD}.",
              visible: CUTN,
              highlighted: ["KN","CF","KH","CD"] },
            { text: "Therefore the remainder {NH} is the same part of the remainder {FD}",
              visible: REMN,
              highlighted: ["NH","FD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "NH is the same part of FD", ref: "VII.7" }] },
            { text: "that the whole {KH} is of the whole {CD}.",
              visible: REMN,
              highlighted: ["KH","CD"] },
            { text: "But the remainder {MK} was proved to be the same part of the remainder {FD}",
              visible: REMN,
              highlighted: ["MK","FD"] },
            { text: "that the whole {GK} is of the whole {CD},",
              visible: REMN,
              highlighted: ["GK","CD"] },
            { text: "therefore the sum of {MK} and {NH} is the same parts of {DF}",
              visible: REMN,
              highlighted: ["MK","NH","FD"] },
            { text: "that the whole {HG} is of the whole {CD}.",
              visible: REMN,
              highlighted: ["GH","CD"] },
            { text: "But the sum of {MK} and {NH} equals {EB}, and {HG} equals {BA},",
              visible: REMN,
              highlighted: ["MK","NH","EB","GH","AB"] },
            { text: "therefore the remainder {EB} is the same parts of the remainder {FD}",
              visible: REMN,
              highlighted: ["EB","FD"] },
            { text: "that the whole {AB} is of the whole {CD}.",
              visible: REMN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD"] },
            { text: "Therefore, if a number is the same parts of a number that a subtracted number is of a subtracted number,",
              visible: REMN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","AE","CF"] },
            { text: "then the remainder is also the same parts of the remainder that the whole is of the whole.",
              visible: REMN,
              highlighted: ["EB","FD","AB","CD"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "VII.8") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "VII.7": "/elements/books/bookVII/propositions/propVII7/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Make {GH} equal to {AB}.

Therefore {AE} is the same parts of {CF} that {GH} is of {CD}.

Divide {GH} into the parts of {CD}, namely {GK} and {KH}, and divide {AE} into the parts of {CF}, namely {AL} and {LE}. Then the multitude of {GK} and {KH} equals the multitude of {AL} and {LE}.

Now since {AL} is the same part of {CF} that {GK} is of {CD}, and {CD} is greater than {CF}, therefore {GK} is also greater than {AL}.

Make {GM} equal to {AL}.

Then {GK} is the same part of {CD} that {GM} is of {CF}. Therefore the remainder {MK} is the same part of the remainder {FD} that the whole {GK} is of the whole {CD}. [!just VII.7]

Again, since {EL} is the same part of {CF} that {KH} is of {CD}, and {CD} is greater than {CF}, therefore {HK} is also greater than {EL}.

Make {KN} equal to {EL}.

Therefore {KN} is the same part of {CF} that {KH} is of {CD}. Therefore the remainder {NH} is the same part of the remainder {FD} that the whole {KH} is of the whole {CD}. [!just VII.7]

But the remainder {MK} was proved to be the same part of the remainder {FD} that the whole {GK} is of the whole {CD}, therefore the sum of {MK} and {NH} is the same parts of {DF} that the whole {HG} is of the whole {CD}.

But the sum of {MK} and {NH} equals {EB}, and {HG} equals {BA}, therefore the remainder {EB} is the same parts of the remainder {FD} that the whole {AB} is of the whole {CD}.

Therefore, *if a number is the same parts of a number that a subtracted number is of a subtracted number, then the remainder is also the same parts of the remainder that the whole is of the whole.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide:

This proposition says multiplication by fractions distributes over subtraction. Algebraically,

<center>(<i>m/n</i>)<i>b</i> + (<i>m/n</i>)<i>e,</i> = (<i>m/n</i>)(<i>b</i> + <i>e</i>).</center>

The sample value taken for *m/n* in the proof is 2/3.

This proposition is used in @VII.11.
